{"_id":"47d34e0a-7f8a-4027-ade9-0dc5a0b41df6","name":"Between the Ages","pages":[{"_id":"tAfbSIaziTPvueOL","name":"Between the Ages","type":"text","title":{"show":false,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRoll d66\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eRoll\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eResult\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e1\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou suffered a great failure and must re-pledge your Oath in order to retain your Knighthood.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou have been in a nearby Realm on diplomatic duty. Roll a Spirit Save. On a pass, you are now well-esteemed there. On a fail you triggered a war with them.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e3\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou have become deathly ill. You that know you will die before the next Age without supernatural intervention.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e4\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou saved the life of a Seer, so they owe you a favour.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e5\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou have been named as heir to a Seat of Power.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e6\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou gain an especially loyal pet.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e7\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eThe most important non-player character to you dies suddenly. You are with them in their last moments.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e8\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou have spent years trapped in an Otherworld.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e9\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou brokered peace with raiders from beyond your borders, who have set up a Holding of their own in the Realm.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e10\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou won a great battle. Choose its location and roll a Vigour Save. On a pass you won, placing a Monument there. Otherwise you lost, placing a Curse there.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e11\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA distant or estranged relative has come to the Realm, finding a place in court.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e12\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eAn enemy or rival from your past has found a place in court.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e13\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou inherit a piece of armour (your choice) belonging to a Knight-Radiant, who has left to find the city. Old knights hold you in high regard when you wear it.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e14\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eRoll a Clarity Save. On a pass you helped depose an unjust ruler, who seeks petty revenge against you. On a fail you unwittingly helped to make them a ruler.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e15\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA defeated foe has placed a sizeable bounty on your head.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e16\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou received prophetic dreams of a new Myth in the realm. The dreams relate to its final Omen.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e17\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou helped a new Seer find their sanctuary. Place it anywhere you wish.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e18\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA random visiting Knight gifts you their steed before they leave.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e19\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eJustifiable or not, the vassals have taken to calling you \u0026quot;The Wicked\u0026quot;\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e20\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eJustifiable or not, the vassals have taken to calling you \u0026quot;The Great\u0026quot;\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e21\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou are offered a new Knightly title. Roll a new Knight type and decide if you wish to exchange your gear and ability for the new one.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e22\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eAs a diplomatic gesture you have been barred from visiting the Seat of Power.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e23\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou fight in a battle that sees the destruction of a random holding. Decide which side you were on.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e24\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou set up a modest home for yourself that has grown into a dwelling. Place it wherever you choose.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e25\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eIllness plagues those close to you. Choose three non-player characters close to you. They must each pass a Vigour Save or die.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e26\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA ghost from a previous encounter still haunts you. You cannot sleep alone.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e27\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou have been exiled from the Realm. If you stay you are doing so under a false identity.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e28\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou were sent to fight against a nearby Realm, earning a bloody reputation amongst its loyal Knights. They swore to come for you one day.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e29\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou helped a young protegee become a full Knight. Roll their Knight type at random, and they are now roaming the Realm on their own quest.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e30\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eTime has been cruel to you. If you are Mature, immediately age to Old. If you are Old, lose d6 Vigour to a minimum of 2.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e31\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eTime has been good to you. If you would age to Old, remain as Mature instead. If you would age to Mature you may increase any one Virtue by d6 to a maximum of 18.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e32\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou earn a reputation in tournaments. Gain d6 Maximum Guard to a maximum of 18.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e33\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYou were embroiled in a blood feud with a ruler of the Realm. Decide somebody close to you who died in the conflict, and also somebody close to them.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e34\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA particularly harrowing battle leaves you with little appetite for combat Lose d6 Maximum Guard to a minimum of 1.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e35\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eAnother Knight bearing your title has entered the Realm, seeking to usurp your position.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003e36\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eA holding unexpectedly fell into your rule.\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e"},"sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":-1},"flags":{}}],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
